Z||000000||adamfiero||11-18-2000||01:11 AM||||my 86 fiero coupe has been overheating and i can't find the problem.  i have a new fan motor and a new water pump, so they both work.  i've flushed out the water system and added new antifreeze.  i've ran the car without the thermostat and it still overheats.  the antifreeze boils over out of the overflow tank, and the car gets really hot and has a dramatic drop in power.  it's been sitting in my yard for about two weeks now, and i want to get my fiero running strong again.  please, if you have any information about this reply soon.  thanks.  my email address is adamfiero@yahoo.com||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT Bastard||11-18-2000||02:25 AM||||Ever heard of the term:  Krack(ed)head?<P>The Fierogod says you've got one of these.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-18-2000||05:48 AM||||Try a compression check for a cracked head. You did "burp" the system when refilling?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rednax Asbestos||11-18-2000||07:27 AM||||Hi Adam,<P>As you can see I'm new here also but I had the same problem with my '86 GT. It turned out to be a lose wire on the fan relay. You said you have a new fan motor but you didn't say wether it turns on or not. If you have a AC then try turning it on. The fan should start running. If not you have an electrical problem. Lets hope its not a cracked head and check the simple thing first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||14
Z||000004||theogre||11-18-2000||12:33 PM||||you definatly need a fan function check. the AC should activate it. if you don't have AC find the temp sensor with only one wire. ground that wire to the block. that should turn on the fan. if neither work you have a fan problem still. (Note: the fan temp sensor only activates about 235F)<P>The  block/head could be bad. thermostat could be bad. the waterpump could be bad. the belt loose. a coolant line under the car crushed. crap in the system blocking up the radiator. any of these will cause over heat. <P>Plus it has to be filled a certain way. fill it wrong and you'll definatly over heat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||adamfiero||11-18-2000||08:26 PM||||@*&%^#!!!!!  i think it is a cracked head.  because everything else is checkin out ok.  fan works, pump works, my hoses aren't blocked up, i don't know about "burping" the system, but newayz...theogre, what u mean by filling it wrong?  u just pour it down there don't ya?  (and make sure any air is out)<P>how much is this gonna cost to fix? (cracked head) or would it be better to part my car out?||||reg||8
