Z||000007||stimpy||11-18-2000||10:26 PM||||Whoa hoss, don't blow it up yet! I've got a set of V6 heads sitting in the garage here in OKC.  Yours for the grabbing.  You may want to get some porting work done while they are off, but I wager they'd work as-is.  It would be a little bit of wrenching to replace yours, but less then tearing up your car.<P>Oh, maybe you've got a 4cyl?  In that case, I know a guy who is getting a SC 3.8 put in his 88 coupe.  You might be able to hook up his tuff for cheap. In any event, I can't imagine finding a head for a 2.5 would be hard||||reg||1
